---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import { rel, SUPPORT_EMAIL, LEGAL_NAME } from '../../consts';
const description = `Privacy policy for Dudley Catalog Prep by ${LEGAL_NAME}.`;
---
<Base title="Privacy Policy · Catalog Prep" description={description} path="/privacy/catalog-prep">
  <main class="page">
    <div class="wrap" style="max-width:720px;">
      <a class="back" href={rel('/privacy/')}>← All privacy policies</a>
      <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="updated">Dudley Catalog Prep · Effective date: September 25, 2026</p>

      <h2>The short version</h2>
      <p>
        {LEGAL_NAME} operates Dudley Catalog Prep ("Catalog Prep"), a service that turns supplier
        catalog files into clean import files for an online store. You use it through an AI assistant
        that connects to it, such as ChatGPT, Claude, Grok, or Meta Muse. We keep the files you upload
        and the files we produce only long enough to do the job (at most 7 days), you can delete them
        sooner, and deleting always needs your own approval. We don't sell your data, we don't show
        ads, we don't run analytics, and no AI model processes your files on our side.
      </p>
      <p>
        Catalog Prep is currently a <strong>prototype for sample data</strong>. Please don't upload
        real customer, personal, or confidential business data while it is a prototype.
      </p>

      <h2>Signing in</h2>
      <p>
        When an assistant connects to Catalog Prep, you sign in through our sign-in provider, Auth0
        (Okta). Auth0 handles your email address, password or passkey, and sign-in times. Catalog Prep
        itself does not store your email address: it receives a verified account identifier and keeps
        only a keyed hash of it, plus the account's permissions. Each connected assistant gets its own
        access that you can end at any time (see "Disconnecting assistants" below).
      </p>

      <h2>Files you upload and files we produce</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>What:</strong> the supplier file and store template you upload, and the results we
          produce from them (an import file, a list of fields we could not fill in, a summary, and a
          manifest with file checksums).</li>
        <li><strong>How they are processed:</strong> by a fixed set of rules. No AI model reads or
          processes your files on our side, and we never use your files to train models.</li>
        <li><strong>Where:</strong> file contents are stored encrypted in Amazon Web Services (S3,
          United States, us-west-2). Job details such as status, sizes, and checksums are stored in a
          database hosted by Railway.</li>
        <li><strong>How long:</strong> a finished job's files are kept for 7 days and then removed
          automatically, unless you delete them sooner.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Deleting your files</h2>
      <p>
        You can ask your assistant to delete a job at any time. Deletion is permanent, so it always needs
        your own approval: the assistant gives you a link, and you sign in with a passkey and approve in
        your browser. Deletion removes the uploaded files, the processing attempts, and the results. A
        small receipt remains that records that the job existed and was deleted; it contains no file
        contents. Copies held in our storage providers' own backup systems may persist for a limited time
        until those backups expire.
      </p>

      <h2>Activity records</h2>
      <p>
        For security and accountability we keep a record of actions taken on your account, such as
        uploading a file, preparing a job, reading a result, approving a deletion, or disconnecting
        assistants. Each record holds the action, the time, the outcome, a request identifier, keyed
        hashes of your account and of the connecting app, and the name of the assistant as that
        assistant reports it. These records contain no file contents.
      </p>

      <h2>AI assistants</h2>
      <p>
        When you use Catalog Prep through an assistant, that assistant's provider (for example OpenAI,
        Anthropic, xAI, or Meta) receives what you share with it and the results Catalog Prep returns to
        it, including the contents of any result file you ask it to read. The provider handles that
        information under its own terms and privacy policy, not this one.
      </p>

      <h2>Who we share data with</h2>
      <p>We use these service providers only to run Catalog Prep:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Auth0 (Okta)</strong>: sign-in and account permissions.</li>
        <li><strong>Amazon Web Services</strong>: encrypted file storage.</li>
        <li><strong>Railway</strong>: hosting and the job database.</li>
        <li><strong>Cloudflare</strong>: domain name service for mcp.dudleyapps.com.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        We don't sell your data, share it for advertising, or combine it with data from our other apps.
        We may disclose information if the law requires it.
      </p>

      <h2>Disconnecting assistants</h2>
      <p>
        You can cut off every assistant at once from the
        <a href="https://mcp.dudleyapps.com/v1/deletion-approvals/disconnect">disconnect page</a>.
        Tokens they already hold stop working immediately, and an assistant can reconnect only after you
        sign in again. You can also remove Catalog Prep from an assistant's own connector settings.
      </p>

      <h2>Security</h2>
      <p>
        Connections use HTTPS/TLS, stored files are encrypted, each account can reach only its own jobs,
        and deletions require a fresh passkey sign-in. No system is perfectly secure, but we take
        reasonable measures to protect your data.
      </p>

      <h2>Children</h2>
      <p>
        Catalog Prep is a business tool and is not directed at children. We do not knowingly collect
        personal information from anyone under 18.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes</h2>
      <p>
        If this policy changes materially, the new version will be posted at this URL with an updated
        date above.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>Questions or data requests? Email <a href={`mailto:${SUPPORT_EMAIL}`}>{SUPPORT_EMAIL}</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </main>
</Base>
